    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "but rebuilding requires something to build with. i don't have that foundation anymore. the \"new path\" everyone talks about just feels like a consolation prize. it's hard to care about \"rebuilding\" when the person who was supposed to live that life is dead. it feels like i'm just waiting for the world to realize i'm already gone. does it ever stop being so exhausting? just existing as a shadow of someone else?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
